From 307d0add8a600c346f55a720598284d888d604cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:39:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Client portal: permanent Rejected tab, paged
 Approved/Posted/Rejected

The Approved / Posted / Rejected tabs shared one request capped at 100 rows
(newest first, mixed with statuses no tab shows), so older tasks vanished,
the tab counts undercounted, and a failed request silently showed 0.

- /api/tasks (client role): new ?clientRejected=1 (every task the client ever
  rejected, any status except HIDDEN, newest rejection first), ?withTotal=1
  (paging.total / hasMore, stable id tiebreak, no title re-sort) and
  ?clientCounts=1 (exact tab badge counts in one grouped query)
- /api/tasks: a real client can no longer point ?clientId= at another client;
  the override only applies to an admin/manager previewing as client
- useClientTasks: per-tab paged lists (useSWRInfinite), lazy-loaded when a tab
  is opened, exact server counts, per-tab error + retry
- ClientDashboard: Rejected tab is a permanent history (not status-filtered),
  "Load more" paging, error state with Retry; approve / request-revisions only
  for CLIENT_REVIEW tasks so a task mid-fix can't be approved from the portal
- ClientTaskCard: current-stage chip, rejection count and Final revision mark
  on the Rejected tab
- scripts/backfill-client-rejections-all-time.sql: rebuilds rejection counts
  from the audit log for all months and statuses (the existing script only
  covers the current month's open tasks)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
